THOUGHT: The NullAway error is due to directly unboxing a potentially null value from the map. I should safely extract `subWorkflowVersion` as an `Object`, handle the null case (likely defaulting to 1, which is common for workflow versions, or using 0 if that’s the existing convention), and also handle non-Integer types (e.g., String or Number) to avoid ClassCast issues. After updating the code, I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm that the specific NullAway error is gone and that the total error count decreased by one without introducing new errors.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/conductor && sed -i '59s/int version = (int) input.get("subWorkflowVersion");/Object subWorkflowVersionObj = input.get("subWorkflowVersion");
        int version;
        if (subWorkflowVersionObj == null) {
            version = 1;
        } else if (subWorkflowVersionObj instanceof Number) {
            version = ((Number) subWorkflowVersionObj).intValue();
        } else {
            version = Integer.parseInt(subWorkflowVersionObj.toString());
        }/' core/src/main/java/com/netflix/conductor/core/execution/tasks/SubWorkflow.java && ./gradlew conductor-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

